{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig","id":1028250,"title":"Home of the Strig","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-07T13:24:14-08:00","id":1028250,"title":"Home of the Strig","content":"Obviously I'm well aware that this thread will be highly speculative!... but I often wonder, what do you imagine the 'Home' of the Strig is like?<br /> <br /> Is it a 'hell' of sorts, some sort of reflection of our own world yet more creepy and shadowy?<br /> <br /> Is it another dimension, with another 'set' (to abuse set theory) which requires unique senses and shadowy physiology to even see it?<br /> <br /> Is it the Abyss of Mage, or some realm within the Mage cosmology?<br /> <br /> Would it be basically a big dark empty space, or would it have features?<br /> <br /> Do you think the shadowy owls that live in that place have identity or culture, or do you imagine they take on these traits when separated from 'home?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T13:42:47-08:00","id":1028254,"title":"","content":"I don't imagine it as a place at all, more of a swirling cloud of strix in no place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:54:02-08:00","id":1028285,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine that the Strix come from a not place and the not place is a place full of shadowy entities other than the strix; this not place is where the void creatures that can be summoned via Cruac come from. Now this not place may come from the Abyss or possibly be a lower depth, and that'd depend on what would work best for the Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T15:46:37-08:00","id":1028301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1028254#post1028254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't imagine it as a place at all, more of a swirling cloud of strix in no place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I kind of picture it as a nonplace of pure darkness and hunger, from which individual Stirges can sometimes split off and enter our world through the Dark Places.<br /> <br /> A Mage might call it a Lower Depth devoid of Life, which it steals from our world in the form of Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T16:57:26-08:00","id":1028333,"title":"","content":"The book says they're not Spriits or Ghosts but I like to lump them in with Mage type Abyssal entities as all the other info about them screams Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T20:32:19-08:00","id":1028405,"title":"","content":"Here's a story I put together (I think I've mentioned it in other topics), combining stuff from Mythologies, BtP, and VtR.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Before the Great Flood, when the world was still intact, young, and unfinished, the gods wished to bring fourth the means of punishing mortal transgressions over their divine word. They sent the Serpent from their midst to seek humanity, in the Gardens between Heaven and Earth, and taint its form. Brother attacked brother and bit him like a serpent until the soul was ripped apart from the flesh. So it was that the form of murder descended, from Above Below, and men turned clubs and stones against their fellow men.<br /> <br /> But those who tasted the blood of their brethren only felt their thirst grow stronger, seeking nectars sweeter than what they could find running through mortal veins. The gods grew fearful, and cast murder\u2019s form away from Creation, deep into the darkest parts of the Shadows and into the land called Nod. Therein it dwelt, itself blameless, among the shadow demons and the other horrors banished from the sight of gods. Murder fought these monsters nightly for whatever little sustenance it could come across, until the land itself changed it into a wandering demon of the plains known of Nod, and it came to be known as Lil\u00fb.<br /> <br /> One night, Lil\u00fb was overcome with the smell of divinity mixed with blood and flesh most pleasant. Following its excited senses, it crossed the desserts of Nod, reaching a woman of unprecedented beauty. The Owls had gotten to her first, their talons and beaks stained and dripping with Vitae sucked out of her empty eye sockets and wounds on her immaculate skin. The woman spoke to Lil\u00fb, her speech overwhelmed with torment.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo not pity me, wanderer. For unlike you, I will one night leave this place.\u201d she told it, struggling in agony for the air that crafted these words.<br /> <br /> The demon did not speak, as denizens of Nod were not accustomed to human speech. It only stared at the woman with perverted lust and primal fear in its eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cHave me, if you wish, so that I may carry your seed out of this land and end your exile, as well as mine.\u201d she told him, her hollow eyes acknowledging Lil\u00fb as it nodded.<br /> <br /> The woman slowly moved her legs apart invitingly. Lil\u00fb approached her, and the two became one, as the owls bit deeper into the woman\u2019s flesh. Her terrible screams, and the screeches and sounds of the owl\u2019s wings, drowned Murder\u2019s moans of release. Her new consort breathing heavily over her, the woman let out ecstatic laughter as her eyes turned a bloody red. The seed she now bore was the Serpent\u2019s.<br /> <br /> She was now Lilith, mistress and mother to all birthed, or commanded in Nod, by Lil\u00fb. Murder now stood powerless before the demons of this land who once feared him.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow leave.\u201d she said, pushing Lil\u00fb away; \u201cMy children wish to feast upon me.\u201d.<br /> <br /> The details of Lil\u00fb\u2019s eventual escape from Nod are unclear. Only a story exists, telling us that it returned to Creation as it had first entered it, arising once more from dirt and fertile soil. Though Lilith was twice-damned, once by the Owls and once by the Serpent, it was Lil\u00fb and those who shared in his sin, that suffered most from the dangers that awaited them beyond Nod. Like their Dark Father, the Earth would reject his children, first under a crescent moon between the two rivers that birthed civilization. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 01-07-2017, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T22:21:05-08:00","id":1028433,"title":"","content":"What's all this then? Oh, I <i>see</i>, you're all making that old neonate mistake vis-a-vis thinking that Strix are properly speaking <i>a thing</i>.<br /> <br /> The truth is that they are <i>holes</i> - a grand assortment of owlish maws, feeding on life and sin.<br /> <br /> Dark Places isn't them returning home - it's just the thing on the other side <i>opening wide</i>. Pray you never see it smile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T22:32:58-08:00","id":1028437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1028301#post1028301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a Lower Depth devoid of Life, which it steals from our world in the form of Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1028433#post1028433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> they are <i>holes</i> - a grand assortment of owlish maws, feeding on life and sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tomato, tomahto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T00:05:08-08:00","id":1028451,"title":"","content":"I think of it as a place of primordial nothing and darkness. How Strix multiply suggests, to me, what the places is. One big ball of nothing from which sometimes Strix break off like water drops. And they can just as easily return to their source.<br /> <br /> I don't like giving things roots in Mage cosmology, though. Mage has its own antagonists. Let other splats have theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T04:00:02-08:00","id":1028489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1028451#post1028451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think of it as a place of primordial nothing and darkness. How Strix multiply suggests, to me, what the places is. One big ball of nothing from which sometimes Strix break off like water drops. And they can just as easily return to their source.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I like the how you described the home of the Strix, and I'll have to keep that in mind for my next Chronicle.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1028451#post1028451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like giving things roots in Mage cosmology, though. Mage has its own antagonists. Let other splats have theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I understand that feeling. I think it stems from the big three world of darkness games (Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage) being likely for tables to play all three games. Lots of people try to find a way to make the settings fit together, and Mage is abstract enough for the other two to fall under Mage cosmology. I tend to try and keep mages from being the supreme authority on the world of darkness, but sometimes their terminology bleeds in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T04:10:09-08:00","id":1028494,"title":"","content":"If it helps, mages don't really understand the lower depths all that well. Most of the weird places get shoved in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:25:33-08:00","id":1028537,"title":"","content":"Eh, everything's fine I guess. To me, the answer depends on one question : How do we want to use it and the strix in general ? If the strix are just going to be the shadowy menace that's more or less defined, then, the shadow realm can be some kind of negative space of owls from which pieces break occasionally and become strix.<br /> <br /> But it can be other things depending on what's needed for the game. You might be tempted to send players there. Would a strix accept to use dark places to let them in, or would it be a trap, meaning the next games would be them trying to escape ? Then, you'd have to start thinking about how it's actually like there. Why do the strix come to our world ? Is it better than the shadow realm, which might be like a super boring dead zone ? Why would they be tempted to go back to it, then (using Dark Places) ? Are strix tourists, who come to our world to fuck shit up like people can go to Las Vegas to blow money and go home broke ? Are the strix drawn back to their home ? Is it some sort of nostalgia of being part of a primordial shadow thingy, an actual compulsion, like what drives changelings to go to Arcadia once they're all grown up ?<br /> <br /> Personnally, while I didn't map out the shadow realm in any way, I like to think there is some sort of society with its own hierarchy there. Probably just based on how big and powerful the strix are. It's kind of mundane, sure, but it's relatable enough that they can be characters whose shoes I can put myself into as a GM. I don't see the shadow realm as much of a &quot;place&quot;, but the way I used it in my last game, it was home to, like, giant strix. Strix old and powerful enough to make other strix obey them, venerate them actually. They're too big to pass through, though. I made Hantu one of those. A huge strix that came to earth long ago, became OP a,d eventually used Dark Places to go back to the shadows to take its place among the shadow gods. Now, it's decided vampires had to go and it wants to come back. It can't just open a portal, though, so it sends smaller strix to set things up for its return. It's basically owl Cthulhu, its shadow potency doesn't really register anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T10:21:22-08:00","id":1028602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1028451#post1028451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like giving things roots in Mage cosmology, though. Mage has its own antagonists. Let other splats have theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, I did say &quot;A Mage might call it&quot; for a reason. Mages like to contextualize things within their frame of reference. The term &quot;Lower Depth&quot; is little more than a shorthand Mages use for &quot;place that doesn't easily fit within the cosmos as we understand it.&quot; That a Mage calls a place a Lower Depth doesn't really mean much, beyond the fact that they didn't know what else to call it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:19:32-08:00","id":1028613,"title":"","content":"one of the options I use for Dis (as I call the strix' world) is a graveyard of the gods- that is where the dead immortals are buried, and from their gaping wounds the blood flows endlessly. From those rivers of ichor the Owls are birthed, and they carry the hunger of their dead masters to the world of the living in order to help those fallen divinities keep a semblance of life.<br /> <br /> That is, of course, only one option for Dis which I use. I switch its exact nature from time to time, just to keep things fresh :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:44:28-08:00","id":1029057,"title":"","content":"Here is an option I came up with!<br /> <br /> The Strix do not remember where they come from but it is a world unlike our own - a world that cannot be explored with our senses, and our bodies. It is therefore difficult to explain but suffice it to say it does have 'things' and 'locations' - it is not just an empty, dark world. No human eyes could see these things just as no human can really understand what a Cuttlefish perceives. It is a world suited for, and inhabited by, shadow-things.<br /> <br /> When a Strix is wanders into our world, they do not remember where they come from. They enter into a world which is unsuited to the senses they are born with. Essentially they become blinded but do not remember ever being able to see. Thus, they become addicted to the senses of living things and corpses. Unable to 'feel', they desire nothing more than to usurp the feelings of others.<br /> <br /> If a Strix was to be returned to the Darkness, they would be astonished at how well suited they were to it, like a fish being returned to the ocean after living in a bowl for a long time. This is why many Strix elect to return to the Darkness when they have the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:04:46-08:00","id":1029310,"title":"","content":"Very nice Piff.<br /> On a related note is Graemalkin from Skinchangers p102 a Strix or related being? It has a shadow form, a shadow pocket dimension home and an owl form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:09:00-08:00","id":1029315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1029310#post1029310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very nice Piff.<br /> On a related note is Graemalkin from Skinchangers p102 a Strix or related being? It has a shadow form, a shadow pocket dimension home and an owl form.</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably weren't when the writers were working on them. Can't be sure, so don't quote me on that. However, the similarity is indeed uncanny... Perhaps the Owls aren't the only residents of this &quot;dark place&quot; after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:15:09-08:00","id":1029319,"title":"","content":"That's Shadow pocket dimension home. Referring to the Hisil.<br /> <br /> 'As the darkness rose up, she could only point, too shocked to scream. The inky cloud writhed, and for a moment the shape of a giant black owl spread its wings behind Marcus. The inky wingspan folded in on itself, and the darkness swirled, stretched, melted into an inky black human shape. Graemalkin stepped forward, extending one hand toward her, and Jennifer suddenly regained her ability to scream.'<br /> <br /> It certainly does seem strix-like. I love the image that came with it. It really seems bent on depicting them as spirits, but you could have it as a strix-spirit amalgam, not quite having the powers and abilities of both, but instead a mixture of thematic similarities.<br /> <br /> Also, \u201cI\u2019m not sure this is such a great idea, Marcus.\u201d Sharp one, that Jennifer. Not sharp enough to not go through with it but still. I imagine it's a very archetypal Chronicles of Darkness scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:22:06-08:00","id":1029323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1029319#post1029319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Shadow pocket dimension home. Referring to the Hisil.<br /> <br /> 'As the darkness rose up, she could only point, too shocked to scream. The inky cloud writhed, and for a moment the shape of a giant black owl spread its wings behind Marcus. The inky wingspan folded in on itself, and the darkness swirled, stretched, melted into an inky black human shape. Graemalkin stepped forward, extending one hand toward her, and Jennifer suddenly regained her ability to scream.'<br /> <br /> It certainly does seem strix-like. I love the image that came with it. It really seems bent on depicting them as spirits, but you could have it as a strix-spirit amalgam, not quite having the powers and abilities of both, but instead a mixture of thematic similarities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they're like the Tengu of Tokyo, which are thought to be Strix but slightly <i>off</i>, enough to be different beings altogether?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, \u201cI\u2019m not sure this is such a great idea, Marcus.\u201d Sharp one, that Jennifer. Not sharp enough to not go through with it but still. I imagine it's a very archetypal Chronicles of Darkness scene. </div> </div> </div>Archetypical? I say essential <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:46:22-08:00","id":1029336,"title":"","content":"Sometimes the player with a bit of sense doesn't want to ruin the others fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T17:15:07-08:00","id":1029355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1028333#post1028333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says they're not Spriits or Ghosts but I like to lump them in with Mage type Abyssal entities as all the other info about them screams Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Strix are not Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T01:55:05-08:00","id":1029508,"title":"","content":"Love the hypotheses presented so far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would probably use the &quot;Strix come from a Non-Place that lacks life, vitality, and substance&quot;, but for the sake of creativity I'm going to go wild here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Strix come not from another dimension, but from the Torpor Dreams of vampires. That's right, the Strix are living nightmares of the dead. Like, all of the dead. Their realm is the Corpse Dream, the rotting shadow of the Astral Realm that suffuses our universe. The Owls then are just like the Beast, in fact perhaps there are Kindred still in Torpor after their Beast flew through the cracks in the world on wings of dark smoke. What fitful dreams they must have in the darkness, without an Owl to lead them back to the world of the living. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T03:00:22-08:00","id":1029525,"title":"","content":"Well. Since we're discussing these alternatives and whatnot, I would tweak Dusk's own idea. That they're not so much dreams or the Beast escaped randomly, but the Beast as unleashed when a vampire dies. Consider that they don't leave behind ghosts because the man is often held to be damned. What then, of the Beast? An interesting thought, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T08:42:38-08:00","id":1029612,"title":"","content":"There's vampire ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T01:51:46-08:00","id":1029966,"title":"","content":"and what if, instead of being escaped beasts of dead vampires or dreams of sleeping ancients, the strixs are, well, vampires? I mean, the vampire clans lack any singular origin, and each such breed of vampires grows apart by itself- until, as times goes on, they start to change, transform and evolve into the more familiar form of &quot;Clans&quot;. While at that state they are quit similar enough to each other (they Embrace the same, feed, the same, can learn each other's powers, etc)- they are still different. But what if that is not the end of their evolution? What if the Curse keeps changing and twisting, turning them into a more unified form of an &quot;ultimate predator&quot;? They grow beyond their humanity, and become the Beast. What if the Owls didn't destroyed the Julii- but simply helped them to ascend to the next level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T03:17:41-08:00","id":1029983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1028451#post1028451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like giving things roots in Mage cosmology, though. Mage has its own antagonists. Let other splats have theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Lower Depths&quot; are only Mage cosmology in the sense that mages are the ones with a generic term for them - a term that essentially means &quot;scary hungry places we don't understand.&quot; Making the Strix home dimension one of them doesn't give Mage any sort of authority over Vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, hypothesis: there is no such realm. Strix are native to Earth, coalescences of twisted, broken, and poisoned life force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:10:41-08:00","id":1029994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1029983#post1029983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> coalescences of twisted, broken, and poisoned life force.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit too werewolf though. And not even the <i>right</i><i> ones. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:24:27-08:00","id":1029998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1029994#post1029994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a bit too werewolf though. And not even the <i>right</i><i> ones. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? How?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:28:47-08:00","id":1029999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1029983#post1029983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Lower Depths&quot; are only Mage cosmology in the sense that mages are the ones with a generic term for them - a term that essentially means &quot;scary hungry places we don't understand.&quot; Making the Strix home dimension one of them doesn't give Mage any sort of authority over Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until a Mage supplement comes out saying X applies to all creatures from this realm and Mage spells can replicate it. Or a new Mage faction has the special ability to command or insta banish or convert to mana or are immune to the special abilities of the denizens from that area. (That's exactly what happens in new supplements.) and all of a sudden it becomes official that this group turns the Vampire Big Bad that no kindred faction can beat into their bitches. It can and most certainly will result in dick measuring contests about the superiority of the Mage line and their themes over Vampire and their themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T05:46:13-08:00","id":1030013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1029998#post1029998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? How?</div> </div> </div> </div>You basically just described the antagonists of Werewolf the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1029999#post1029999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until a Mage supplement comes out saying X applies to all creatures from this realm and Mage spells can replicate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not going to happen for a lower depth. They're defined by magic <i>not</i> working. In this case, the Life arcarnum is null and void. Other than that they work just like everything else as far as magic is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-11-2017, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T05:57:57-08:00","id":1030016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1030013#post1030013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You basically just described the antagonists of Werewolf the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. I'm talking about strix being creatures of pure vitae, and since both other vitae-bearing species - humans and vampires - are native to the physical world, suggesting that strix be too, with no other &quot;realm of origin.&quot; I don't see what's so WtA about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1029999#post1029999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can and most certainly will result in dick measuring contests about the superiority of the Mage line and their themes over Vampire and their themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what? In all my times on these forums, I've seen <i>one</i> such dick-measuring comment come from someone championing Mage. Every single other time has been from people hating on it. And as Elfive said, there's never going to be a Mage supplement about how mages awesome all over strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 01-11-2017, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:35:42-08:00","id":1030045,"title":"","content":"This is what I use for my Homebrew<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark is the native otherworldly place of Strix and Tengu. It is where they can vanish to and come forth from if they are so inclined and empowered. Defining the Dark as a place or world is skirting several implications made by those words because the Dark, while it is usually spoken of as a location when it is described by those that know of it, lacks many qualities of anything else labeled a place, location, or world.<br /> Nothing outside nor inside the Dark can sense anything within the Dark. Within the Dark there is no sense of space, time, matter, other beings within the Dark, or even one\u2019s own body. Without these it is hard to say movement or travel happens but while in the Dark a being is just a consciousness experiencing a profoundly deep blackness. Beings in the Dark with the ability to sense things without light can shift their perceptions to what seem to be windows of sensory input from the places of absolute darkness which are Resonant with being enervated of life force, such as the corpses left from vampire feeding sealed in a shallow grave, the husks left by Reaper Mages locked in a lightless cell, the area between the walls that affected by a miasma of siphoned of vitality caused by unspeakable life-draining horrors, ect... These area are where beings that have the Gate Manifestation as it relates to the Dark, which is built upon an Opening the aforementioned Resonant Condition, can cross over. Beings native to the Dark naturally are in Twilight in the Material world and are visible but incorporeal to vampires, being on the same metaphysical frequency but not physical beings themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1030103#post1030103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any exploration takes place on the homeworld of the Strix, I'd rather it is kept strictly from the viewpoint of Vampires. It would be fun to finally get some insight into how Kindred explore and perceive of the various realms of CofD. Keeping them anchored in the material contradicts the common practice I've seen taking place around tables.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly agree with this, and is why I've made the Dark in the way I have and am currently Homebrewing the flattening of the power stats to instead be being pulled out of the material world as high ranking Ephemeral beings are, making Methuselah vampires caught in cycles of blood-thinning torpor that if they break leads them to being drawn into Dark, only able to escape based on Conditions, like Ephemeral beings. (Doing the same with the other splats at power stat 6 or above for their particular otherworlds)<br /> <br /> I also use the various power sources Vitae, Mana, Essense, Plasm, Glamour, ect... for the appropriate Ephemeral being and to determine what physical beings are on the same &quot;frequency&quot; to see them in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-16-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T09:56:38-08:00","id":1030103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1030016#post1030016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, no. I'm talking about strix being creatures of pure vitae, and since both other vitae-bearing species - humans and vampires - are native to the physical world, suggesting that strix be too, with no other &quot;realm of origin.&quot; I don't see what's so WtA about that.<br /> <br /> You know what? In all my times on these forums, I've seen <i>one</i> such dick-measuring comment come from someone championing Mage. Every single other time has been from people hating on it. And as Elfive said, there's never going to be a Mage supplement about how mages awesome all over strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one? Lucky. [edited, no use in bringing up past examples, but let's just say I've seen both sides hate on the other]<br /> <br /> I get what you're saying though. A number of people hate on Mage just <i>because</i>. Still, the Strix are a Vampire phenomenon, they are attracted to Vampires mostly, and the only Mage group that had a recorded encounter with them was <i>going</i> to be the Tremere (but was changed into the 'Sons of Phobos' eventually).<br /> <br /> If any exploration takes place on the homeworld of the Strix, I'd rather it is kept strictly from the viewpoint of Vampires. It would be fun to finally get some insight into how Kindred explore and perceive of the various realms of CofD. Keeping them anchored in the material contradicts the common practice I've seen taking place around tables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 01-11-2017, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T10:52:01-08:00","id":1030132,"title":"","content":"Since it caused a few comments, I'll clarify:<br /> <br /> My comments on mage cosmology were more in reference to OP's question about Strix and the Abyss, and one other individual who suggested that connection. It wasn't directed at <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>.<br /> <br /> Mages try to categorize things according to their cosmology. That's fine and perfectly in-theme for Mages. But trying to tie Strix, who are the primary antagonists of Vampires, to the Abyss, which is the primary antagonist of Mages, rubs me the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T10:56:59-08:00","id":1030135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1030103#post1030103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you're saying though. A number of people hate on Mage just <i>because</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Context helps. Rather like certain other arguments, a good number of us here were around when there were a lot of vocal people about Mage and how everything fell under their view of the universe, and quite often their power. They were really fucking insistent.<br /> <br /> We don't get a lot of people spewing the supremacy of Mages these days, and that's good, but a large number of us still have this kneejerk reaction from that time where it just happened so damn much.<br /> <br /> So, no, not just because, but because there was a time when quite a few Mage fans could be real jackasses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T00:20:31-08:00","id":1030459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1030135#post1030135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Context helps. Rather like certain other arguments, a good number of us here were around when there were a lot of vocal people about Mage and how everything fell under their view of the universe, and quite often their power. They were really fucking insistent.<br /> <br /> We don't get a lot of people spewing the supremacy of Mages these days, and that's good, but a large number of us still have this kneejerk reaction from that time where it just happened so damn much.<br /> <br /> So, no, not just because, but because there was a time when quite a few Mage fans could be real jackasses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wholeheartedly agree. Such was the example I redacted, so as to avoid tension. Plus, the Tremere should've stayed with Vampire.......... (that's the real life Hermetic in me, not the power player speaking)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T01:44:39-08:00","id":1030473,"title":"","content":"Well, you're half right.<br /> <br /> Most Strix are from the material world. Their mechanics include how they reproduce, and they've been around longer than the clans have.<br /> <br /> That said, there is that one power that opens a shadow to somewhere <i>else</i>, and there's the story in Requiem for Rome about the Julii's founder entering the Strirges' world to make his deal with them.<br /> <br /> Vampires' writers' bible says that that world is what mages call a Lower Depth, but whether it's their home, or just somewhere they can move to after they become Potent enough, who knows?<br /> <br /> When we talk about the Lower Depths in mage, we prefer to invent new ones. When we do bring up Depths created outside Mage, we tend to go for the Inferno, as that's less likely to upset touchy vampire or mummy fans <br /> <br /> <br /> You're wrong about the Tremere, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T02:08:09-08:00","id":1030481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1030473#post1030473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you're half right.<br /> <br /> Most Strix are from the material world. Their mechanics include how they reproduce, and they've been around longer than the clans have.<br /> <br /> That said, there is that one power that opens a shadow to somewhere <i>else</i>, and there's the story in Requiem for Rome about the Julii's founder entering the Strirges' world to make his deal with them.<br /> <br /> Vampires' writers' bible says that that world is what mages call a Lower Depth, but whether it's their home, or just somewhere they can move to after they become Potent enough, who knows?<br /> <br /> When we talk about the Lower Depths in mage, we prefer to invent new ones. When we do bring up Depths created outside Mage, we tend to go for the Inferno, as that's less likely to upset touchy vampire or mummy fans <br /> <br /> <br /> You're wrong about the Tremere, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe, no issue with Mage, it's a game I would've gone for more than Vampire had I found players.<br /> <br /> Just sentimental love for the Tremere and the Sons of Phobos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T02:35:01-08:00","id":1030486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1030459#post1030459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wholeheartedly agree. Such was the example I redacted, so as to avoid tension. Plus, the Tremere should've stayed with Vampire.......... (that's the real life Hermetic in me, not the power player speaking)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly enough, Tremere were mages before they were ever part of Vampire.<br /> <br /> They were originally a House in Ars Magica, a property which White Wolf owned for a time. A House that had a problem with vampire membership as time went on.<br /> <br /> Becoming mages again in CofD is more a return to form than a change of splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T03:33:06-08:00","id":1030503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1030486#post1030486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly enough, Tremere were mages before they were ever part of Vampire.<br /> <br /> They were originally a House in Ars Magica, a property which White Wolf owned for a time. A House that had a problem with vampire membership as time went on.<br /> <br /> Becoming mages again in CofD is more a return to form than a change of splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the Tremere had become recognizable as a Vampire clan from VtM. Them and the Nagaraja moving to Mage left some players without two playable options of sentimental value to the community. That's like merging together all necromantic bloodlines in Requiem, placing their origins in ancient Greek chthonic cults, and calling them Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> It's one of those silly things that mean very little to the actual roleplaying experience, like easter eggs that popped up in a different game than you would expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T05:39:26-08:00","id":1030525,"title":"","content":"It's a parallel. In CoD, instead of becoming mage-like vampires, they became vampire-like mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T06:30:37-08:00","id":1030544,"title":"","content":"There's also a pretty vocal group that absolutely hated both the Nagaraja and the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T14:13:58-08:00","id":1030785,"title":"","content":"Strix? Former vampires who've reached Golconda and discovered it's not all it's cracked up to be...<br /> <br /> Explains their hatred for vampires, habitual lying about origins etc., steering them to evilness, and liking to help/see/make them self destruct.<br /> <br /> How's that for personal horror? Congrats, after centuries of pain and struggle, you've finally ascended your condition and made peace with the universe! <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>NOT</b></span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 01-12-2017, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:38:34-08:00","id":1032762,"title":"","content":"Ghouls can survive visiting the Strix plane, which means it has to be at least habitable for Ghouls, that means air, warm enough they don't freeze to death, something to walk on so they can move about, ect... <br /> <br /> If it's just a giant megastrix, a ghoul would just die and even Vampires would find it hard to nearly impossible to naviagate. <br /> <br /> Also what do the Strix feed on while there? <br /> <br /> Is the Strix Plane and the Void Creature plane the same? Because the little we learned about the Strix Plane in the core book suggests it inhabitable, otherwise visiting it would mean instant death to any ghoul who visited it,, even briefly. <br /> <br /> The Void Creature Plane on the other hand from the fiction and merit seems deadly to none Void Creatures. They could be different locations of the same plane, the Strix dwell on the fringes, Void Creatures in the deadly heart for example, or another explanation entirely. <br /> <br /> Also it doesn't say if Void Creatures have blood potency or shadow potency like Strix.<br /> <br /> Void Creatures also serve Kindred, whereas Strix oppose Vampires usually, although some Strix exploit Vampires instead or make deals with them, but the Strix are never willing servants of Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:00:30-08:00","id":1032775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032762#post1032762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls can survive visiting the Strix plane</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get that idea?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:01:13-08:00","id":1032776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032762#post1032762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls can survive visiting the Strix plane, which means it has to be at least habitable for Ghouls, that means air, warm enough they don't freeze to death, something to walk on so they can move about, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get this information from?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032762#post1032762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also what do the Strix feed on while there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having confirmation now that their place of origin is noted in the writer's bible as being a Lower Depth? Nothing. The place completely lacks the thing they feed on. That's why they want to leave it to come here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032762#post1032762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Strix Plane and the Void Creature plane the same? Because the little we learned about the Strix Plane in the core book suggests it inhabitable, otherwise visiting it would mean instant death to any ghoul who visited it,, even briefly. <br /> <br /> The Void Creature Plane on the other hand from the fiction and merit seems deadly to none Void Creatures. They could be different locations of the same plane, the Strix dwell on the fringes, Void Creatures in the deadly heart for example, or another explanation entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not sure how what we learned about it from the core book suggests it's inhabitable to ghouls. But, in any case, whether or not it and the place Cruac voidmages draw their servants from are the same place is something for the ST to decide. Personally, I would say that they are the same (non)place, but if it suits the story to say they're not, then they shouldn't be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032762#post1032762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it doesn't say if Void Creatures have blood potency or shadow potency like Strix.<br /> <br /> Void Creatures also serve Kindred, whereas Strix oppose Vampires usually, although some Strix exploit Vampires instead or make deals with them, but the Strix are never willing servants of Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the void creatures are stirges, they're probably Shadow Potency 0. Almost more proto-stirges, in the same way Muthra are proto-spirits. They may lack the autonomy to act against the ritualists that summoned them. Besides, they're not totally obedient to their summoners. The Merit does say they rebel in little ways that make the Acolyte's life &quot;interesting&quot;. That may be the most these little proto-stirges are capable of, either due to their own premature state of development or due to the magic of the Cruac style that summons them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:02:34-08:00","id":1032937,"title":"","content":"&quot;Anything with a taint of the Strix\u2019s nature \u2014 Strix, vampires, and ghouls, for example \u2014 may cross over to the Strix\u2019s world entirely by spending a Willpower point. The gateway only stays open for a scene, however, and anyone seeking the ancient Strix must cross back over in time or be lost.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Dark Place wasn't inhabitable by a Ghoul one who spent a willpower point and crossed over to the Dark Place, would simply die, no chance of returning before the scene was over.<br /> <br /> It occurred to me that an interesting inspiration for the Dark Place would be the Upside Down from Stranger Things.<br /> <br /> I actually like the idea of the Dark Place having other assorted horrors then the Strix. <br /> <br /> The idea of proto strix is interesting, but I personally lean towards Void Creatures being a different species within the Dark Place, aside from being shadowy in their natural form, they don't behave like Strix or look like Strix, heck we don't even know how they feed to gain vitae.<br /> <br /> Interesting thought, what if the Strix and the Void Creatures are enemies back in the Dark Place, like they hunt and feed on each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-16-2017, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:29:05-08:00","id":1032945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032937#post1032937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Anything with a taint of the Strix\u2019s nature \u2014 Strix, vampires, and ghouls, for example \u2014 may cross over to the Strix\u2019s world entirely by spending a Willpower point. The gateway only stays open for a scene, however, and anyone seeking the ancient Strix must cross back over in time or be lost.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Dark Place wasn't inhabitable by a Ghoul one who spent a willpower point and crossed over to the Dark Place, would simply die, no chance of returning before the scene was over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Well, there's nothing about the gateway to the Other World from whence the void creatures come that suggests it would be inhospitable to creatures so Tainted as well. It only seems harmful to (and hungry for) living things. In fact, it being opened with a point of Willpower only seems to make the parallel stronger.<br /> <br /> &quot;With a point of Willpower, the gateway, which allows the oddity through, can also absorb others and drag them into a dark place of no return. This only works on living things; the other world doesn\u2019t want for Kindred blood. Choose a victim when using this ability. The victim feels the pull of the unearthly, and must resist or be obliterated.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032937#post1032937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurred to me that an interesting inspiration for the Dark Place would be the Upside Down from Stranger Things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I read the Upside Down more as the Hedge, or maybe the Shadow, personally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032937#post1032937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like the idea of the Dark Place having other assorted horrors then the Strix. <br /> <br /> The idea of proto strix is interesting, but I personally lean towards Void Creatures being a different species within the Dark Place, aside from being shadowy in their natural form, they don't behave like Strix or look like Strix, heck we don't even know how they feed to gain vitae.<br /> <br /> Interesting thought, what if the Strix and the Void Creatures are enemies back in the Dark Place, like they hunt and feed on each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. I prefer thinking of them as the Strix equivalent of Muthra and Plasms, but what ever works for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:50:12-08:00","id":1033123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028250-home-of-the-strig?p=1032937#post1032937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Anything with a taint of the Strix\u2019s nature \u2014 Strix, vampires, and ghouls, for example \u2014 may cross over to the Strix\u2019s world entirely by spending a Willpower point. The gateway only stays open for a scene, however, and anyone seeking the ancient Strix must cross back over in time or be lost.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Dark Place wasn't inhabitable by a Ghoul one who spent a willpower point and crossed over to the Dark Place, would simply die, no chance of returning before the scene was over.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily true.<br /> <br /> Similar to Mage's Ghost Gate, or how ephemerals work, the portal could simply change those who pass through to make them more suitable for the environment, or lackthereof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T04:17:50-08:00","id":1033259,"title":"","content":"Technically, human beings can survive in outer space. Not for very long, but they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:51:10-08:00","id":1033325,"title":"","content":"And if there's no time there they can survive indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T22:12:06-08:00","id":1033884,"title":"","content":"I could see it being possible with mages; they essentially break all established rules for humans. The mage in question would have to have the death arcana to count as tainted in my book. However I wouldn't allow a werewol to cross over because their shtick is spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0